# Frontend Components

## File Structure

Each component lives in its own directory:

```
components/SpecCard/
├── index.ts              # Re-export only
├── SpecCard.tsx           # Component implementation
├── SpecCard.module.scss   # BEM styles
└── SpecCard.test.tsx      # Tests
```

## Rules

- Named exports only. No default exports.
- Props interface named `{ComponentName}Props`, exported alongside the component.
- Components are props-driven. No direct store access in leaf/shared components.
- `observer()` wrapping is reserved for container components that read stores.
- Keep components focused — one responsibility each.

## Example

```tsx
import styles from './SpecCard.module.scss';

export interface SpecCardProps {
  title: string;
  status: 'draft' | 'published';
  onSelect: () => void;
}

export function SpecCard({ title, status, onSelect }: SpecCardProps) {
  return (
    <article
      className={`${styles.SpecCard} ${styles['SpecCard--' + status]}`}
      onClick={onSelect}
    >
      <h3 className={styles.SpecCard__Title}>{title}</h3>
      <span className={styles.SpecCard__Badge}>{status}</span>
    </article>
  );
}
```

## Anti-patterns

- Importing a MobX store directly in a shared component.
- Using `React.FC` — declare props as function parameters instead.
- Default exports or anonymous arrow components.
